# SSSF environment. Copy to .env at the target repo root and fill in.
#
# WHICH KEYS YOU NEED DEPENDS ON YOUR ROSTER.
# Every `model:` in adws/adw_sssf_config/sssf.config.yaml is written as
# provider/model-id. The provider half decides which key must be set, and which
# key pi reads for that provider comes from ~/.pi/agent/models.json.
#
# The starter roster names three providers, so it needs three keys:
#   google/gemini-3.6-flash                      served via openrouter -> OPENROUTER_API_KEY
#   fireworks/accounts/fireworks/models/kimi-k3  fireworks             -> FIREWORKS_API_KEY
#   openai/gpt-5.6-terra, openai/gpt-5.6-luna    openai                -> OPENAI_API_KEY
#
# Point every agent at one provider and you only need that provider's key.
# Setting `defaults.model` and deleting the per-agent `model:` overrides is the
# fastest way to run the whole roster on a single key.
#
# Nothing validates this for you. `agents.validate()` checks that a model is
# written as provider/id, not that the provider is reachable or that its key is
# set, so a missing key shows up when that agent runs, not at startup.

# The starter roster as installed needs NONE of these: its pi agents run on
# nousresearch :free models, which pi pays for with the login in
# ~/.pi/agent/auth.json, and its claude agents use the claude CLI's own auth.
# Fill a key in only when you point an agent at that provider.
OPENROUTER_API_KEY=
FIREWORKS_API_KEY=
OPENAI_API_KEY=

# CLAUDE CODE AGENTS need no key here: `claude` uses the auth already on the
# machine (subscription login or ANTHROPIC_API_KEY in your shell). Their
# `model:` is an alias (opus, sonnet, haiku) or a claude-* id, NOT provider/id.

# Optional overrides
# PI_PATH=pi                       # pi binary if not on PATH
# PI_MODELS_PATH=~/.pi/agent/models.json
# ENGINEER_NAME=                   # engineer lane label, defaults to git user.name
# CLAUDE_CODE_PATH=claude          # claude binary if not on PATH
# CLAUDE_PERMISSION_MODE=bypassPermissions
#   How claude answers its own permission prompts. The default matches what pi
#   already does — nobody is at the keyboard, and adw_modules/permissions.py
#   rolls back anything written outside the agent's `writes:` list afterwards.
#   Set acceptEdits to keep claude's own guardrails on Bash; expect stalls.
# CLAUDE_SAFE_MODE=1               # 1 = run claude agents isolated from your own
#   CLAUDE.md, hooks, plugins and skills. Turn it off only if a factory agent is
#   meant to inherit your personal Claude Code setup.
# CLAUDE_MCP_CONFIG=               # path to an MCP config; empty = no MCP servers.
#   Left empty on purpose: a loaded MCP roster put ~67k tokens of tool
#   definitions into every prompt here — $0.79 vs $0.02 for the same Opus turn.
